    },
    "macOS didn’t make %@ the default app for archives, and refused some archive types outright. In Finder, select an archive of each type, choose File > Get Info, pick %@ under “Open with”, then click Change All.": {
      "comment": "Mac Welcome window and Settings: macOS reported success making the app the default for some archive types, but Finder still opens them with another app, and refused other types with an error. Both %@ = the app’s name. File > Get Info, “Open with” and Change All are Finder’s menu item, section and button; keep them as macOS names them.",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS didn’t make %@ the default app for archives, and refused some archive types outright. In Finder, select an archive of each type, choose File > Get Info, pick %@ under “Open with”, then click Change All."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "macOS didn’t make %@ the default app for archives. In Finder, select an archive, choose File > Get Info, pick %@ under “Open with”, then click Change All.": {
      "comment": "Mac Welcome window and Settings: macOS reported success making the app the default for archives, but Finder still opens them with another app. Both %@ = the app’s name. File > Get Info, “Open with” and Change All are Finder’s menu item, section and button; keep them as macOS names them.",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS didn’t make %@ the default app for archives. In Finder, select an archive, choose File > Get Info, pick %@ under “Open with”, then click Change All."
          }
        }
      }
    }
